 /*
- * Compile-only groundwork for the Apple T7000-family PCIe host controller.
+ * Apple T7000-family PCIe -- enable-sequence + generic-enumeration +
+ * PERST + per-port controller window read test.
  *
- * The real J81 ADT describes four ports, four port interrupts and twelve
- * register windows. Corellium's older H9P driver confirms the four-port
- * controller shape, but its register layout, SART and hard-coded PHY sequence
- * are not valid for T7000. The disabled device tree preserves J81's exact
- * resource ordering without naming the unresolved small-window roles. Keep
- * this driver inert until those roles, DART attachment and ADT-provided
- * tunables have been implemented.
+ * Stage 4a of implementing the real host-controller driver. `0035`
+ * (Stage 3: the enable sequence + generic ECAM enumeration + PERST
+ * deassertion) is cross-build verified and awaiting its own hardware
+ * result. Apple's recovered order finishes with one more step this
+ * project hasn't implemented yet: after PERST is deasserted, set bit 0
+ * of the *per-port controller window's* own config register at offset
+ * 0x80 to start the actual link attempt (see
+ * docs/plans/2026-09-13-j81-wifi-pcie.md's "Enable-sequence checkpoint",
+ * step 5).
+ *
+ * That per-port controller window (ADT reg index `2 * port + 1` = 3 for
+ * port 1, physical address 0x602004000, 4 KiB) has never been touched
+ * by any test in this investigation -- every prior register access
+ * (`0019`-`0035`) was either the shared window (reg index 9) or the
+ * ECAM/config-space window (reg index 0), both independently proven
+ * safe to read *and* write across many rounds before this. The
+ * per-port window has had zero prior reads. Following this project's
+ * own established discipline (never write to a register region that
+ * hasn't first been read safely -- see how `0020`/`0021`/`0022`/`0024`
+ * all preceded any write to their respective windows), this stage adds
+ * exactly one new variable: a single bounded, logged *read* of that
+ * window's offset 0x80 (plus offset 0x00 as a baseline sanity check),
+ * still with no write. The actual link-start *write* is deliberately
+ * deferred to a later stage (4b), gated on this read succeeding
+ * cleanly.
+ *
+ * ADT index derivation: docs/plans/2026-09-13-j81-wifi-pcie.md's
+ * register-window table labels ADT entries 1/3/5/7 by the literal
+ * address digit (e.g. entry 3 = 0x602004000 is called "port 2" there,
+ * since "2" appears in the address) -- a different, purely descriptive
+ * convention from Apple's own 0-indexed `port` C variable used
+ * throughout this driver (and already hardware-confirmed: the shared
+ * window's port-1 stride block, offset 0x80 within reg index 9, was
+ * confirmed populated with real non-trivial register values by `0024`).
+ * `AppleEmbeddedPCIEPort` maps controller-window resource `2 * port + 1`
+ * using that same 0-indexed `port` variable, so port 1 (the confirmed
+ * populated port) maps to ADT index 2*1+1 = 3 -- not the doc table's
+ * "port 1" label (index 1), which is address-digit-1, a different port
+ * in Apple's own numbering. This bounded read is itself a direct test
+ * of that derivation: a plausible, non-fault register value here is
+ * evidence the index is right; an obvious fault or implausible pattern
+ * would be evidence to re-derive it before ever writing.
+ *
+ * Everything else is unchanged from Stage 3 -- see that patch's own
+ * header comment for the PERST-deassertion correction, and `0033`'s for
+ * the enable-sequence evidence trail.
  */
 
